hed":"2026-04-21T14:48:55Z","author":{"name":"speckx","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=speckx"}},{"id":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47849315","title":"Fusion Power Plant Simulator","content_html":"\n\u003cp\u003eArticle URL: \u003ca href=\"https://www.fusionenergybase.com/fusion-power-plant-simulator\"\u003ehttps://www.fusionenergybase.com/fusion-power-plant-simulator\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eComments URL: \u003ca href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47849315\"\u003ehttps://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47849315\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePoints: 134\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e# Comments: 81\u003c/p\u003e\n","url":"https://www.fusionenergybase.com/fusion-power-plant-simulator","external_url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47849315","date_published":"2026-04-21T14:26:52Z","author":{"name":"sam","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=sam"}},{"id":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47849221","title":"Brands got worse on purpose","content_html":"\n\u003cp\u003eArticle URL: \u003ca href=\"https://www.worseonpurpose.com/p/your-favorite-brands-got-worse-on-purpose\"\u003ehttps://www.worseonpurpose.com/p/your-favorite-brands-got-worse-on-purpose\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eComments URL: \u003ca href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47849221\"\u003ehttps://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47849221\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePoints: 201\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e# Comments: 156\u003c/p\u003e\n","url":"https://www.worseonpurpose.com/p/your-favorite-brands-got-worse-on-purpose","external_url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47849221","date_published":"2026-04-21T14:19:49Z","author":{"name":"neon_electro","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=neon_electro"}},{"id":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47849097","title":"Show HN: GoModel – an open-source AI gateway in Go","content_html":"\n\u003cp\u003eHi, I’m Jakub, a solo founder based in Warsaw.\u003cp\u003eI’ve been building GoModel since December with a couple of contributors. It's an open-source AI gateway that sits between your app and model providers like OpenAI, Anthropic or others.\u003cp\u003eI built it for my startup to solve a few problems:\u003cp\u003e\u003cpre\u003e\u003ccode\u003e  - track AI usage and cost per client or team\n  - switch models without changing app code\n  - debug request flows more easily\n  - reduce AI spendings with exact and semantic caching\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\nHow is it different?\u003cp\u003e\u003cpre\u003e\u003ccode\u003e  - ~17MB docker image\n    - LiteLLM's image is more than 44x bigger (\"docker.litellm.ai/berriai/litellm:latest\" ~ 746 MB on amd64)\n  - request workflow is visible and easy to inspect    \n  - config is environment-variable-first by default\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\nI'm posting now partly because of the recent LiteLLM supply-chain attack. Their team handled it impressively well, but some people are looking at alternatives anyway, and GoModel is one.\u003cp\u003eWebsite: \u003ca href=\"https://gomodel.enterpilot.io\" rel=\"nofollow\"\u003ehttps://gomodel.enterpilot.io\u003c/a\u003e\u003cp\u003eAny feedback is appreciated.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eComments URL: \u003ca href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47849097\"\u003ehttps://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47849097\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePoints: 155\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e# Comments: 61\u003c/p\u003e\n","url":"https://github.com/ENTERPILOT/GOModel/","external_url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47849097","date_published":"2026-04-21T14:11:53Z","author":{"name":"santiago-pl","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=santiago-pl"}},{"id":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47848276","title":"Anthropic takes $5B from Amazon and pledges $100B in cloud spending in return","content_html":"\n\u003cp\u003eArticle URL: \u003ca href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/20/anthropic-takes-5b-from-amazon-and-pledges-100b-in-cloud-spending-in-return/\"\u003ehttps://techcrunch.com/2026/04/20/anthropic-takes-5b-from-amazon-and-pledges-100b-in-cloud-spending-in-return/\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eComments URL: \u003ca href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47848276\"\u003ehttps://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47848276\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePoints: 254\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e# Comments: 261\u003c/p\u003e\n","url":"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/20/anthropic-takes-5b-from-amazon-and-pledges-100b-in-cloud-spending-in-return/","external_url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47848276","date_published":"2026-04-21T13:08:25Z","author":{"name":"Brajeshwar","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=Brajeshwar"}},{"id":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47848195","title":"Tindie store under \"scheduled maintenance\" for days","content_html":"\n\u003cp\u003eArticle URL: \u003ca href=\"https://www.tindie.com/\"\u003ehttps://www.tindie.com/\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eComments URL: \u003ca href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47848195\"\u003ehttps://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47848195\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePoints: 107\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e# Comments: 57\u003c/p\u003e\n","url":"https://www.tindie.com/","external_url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47848195","date_published":"2026-04-21T13:02:00Z","author":{"name":"somemisopaste","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=somemisopaste"}},{"id":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47847928","title":"The abandoned war: Why no one is stopping the genocide in Sudan","content_html":"\n\u003cp\u003eArticle URL: \u003ca href=\"https://respublica.media/en/en-sudan-abandoned-war-genocide-no-one-stopping/\"\u003ehttps://respublica.media/en/en-sudan-abandoned-war-genocide-no-one-stopping/\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eComments URL: \u003ca href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47847928\"\u003ehttps://news.y